damaged_code:
```rust
let mut done = false;
while !done && has_next() {
    let item = next();
    if item.is_target() {
        process(item);
        done = true;
    }
}
```

fix:
Replace the flag with a break, labeled break, or return at the equivalent exit point. Use return only if exiting the whole function is intended. Preserve work, cleanup, and condition side effects that originally occurred after the assignment or at the next loop test rather than blindly exiting immediately at the assignment:
```rust
while has_next() {
    let item = next();
    if item.is_target() {
        process(item);
        break;
    }
}
```
